{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":1067,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ezek.6","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Ezekiel","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Ezekiel 6","reference":"Ezekiel 6","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"A threatening of the destruction of Israel for their idolatry, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-7.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"A promise of the gracious return of a remnant, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"8-10.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"Directions to lament the sins and calamities of Israel, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"11-14.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":8,"text":"The mountains - The inhabitants of the mountains, who were secure in their fastnesses.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":9,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":10,"text":"Rivers - To those who dwell by river sides, or in the valleys.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":11,"text":"High places - The places of your idolatrous worship.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":13,"text":"Cast down - Before the altars of your idols, which you fly to for refuge.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":14,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":15,"text":"And - Thus the idols were upbraided with their inability to help their worshippers, and the idolaters, with the folly of trusting in them.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":16,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":17,"text":"Your works - All your costly work for your idols.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":18,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":19,"text":"Remnant - It is the Lord that preserves a remnant, the enemies rage would destroy all.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":20,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":21,"text":"Shall remember - So as to turn unto me.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":22,"text":"Broken - I am much grieved.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":23,"text":"Whorish heart - Idolatrous hearts depart from God, as an adulterous wife departs from her husband.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":24,"text":"Loath - With a mixture of grief towards God, of indignation against themselves, and abhorrence of the offense.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":25,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":26,"text":"In vain - Either without cause, the sufferers gave him just cause to pronounce that evil; or without effect.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":27,"text":"Their sins where the cause, and their destruction is the effect of their sufferings.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":28,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":29,"text":"Smite - To shew thy wonder, indignation, sorrow, and pity, for their sins and sufferings.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":30,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":31,"text":"Far off - Either by flight, or captivity.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":32,"text":"Shall fall - Who dwell near to Jerusalem, or would retire to it, when the Babylonians approach.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":33,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":34,"text":"Wilderness - The horrid wilderness of Moab.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":35,"text":"Therein the fiery serpents so much annoyed Israel.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":36,"text":"Accordingly the land of Canaan is at this day one of the most desolate countries in the world.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":6}}